# File contexts for qdistro admin broker.
#
# Phase 2 (0.2.0): labels the broker .py so systemd's exec of the
# script triggers the init_daemon_domain transition into
# qdistro_broker_t. The .py is installed mode 0755 with a
# `#!/usr/bin/env python3` shebang and the unit's ExecStart points
# at the script directly (not at /usr/bin/python3 + arg). The
# kernel reads the shebang, exec's the interpreter, but the
# transition decision is taken on the FIRST execve target — i.e.
# the labelled .py — so the daemon ends up in qdistro_broker_t
# regardless of the python interpreter's own label.
#
# /run/qdistro/* is left unlabelled in Phase 2 — the broker's
# runtime data is still under /var/lib/qdistro/ and /run is touched
# only via per-uid bus sockets mediated by session_dbusd_t. A
# future Phase 3 may move audit DB / cache under /run/qdistro/<uid>/
# and add a regex here.

/usr/libexec/qdistro/qdistro_admin_broker\.py    --  gen_context(system_u:object_r:qdistro_broker_exec_t,s0)
